### 4. XPATH STRATEGIES (MANDATORY PRIORITY)
```python
# Priority 1: ID and Name attributes - HIGHEST STABILITY
element_main = "//input[@id='ElementId' and @name='ElementName']"

# Priority 2: Class with ID/Name combination
element_by_class = "//input[@name='ElementName' and @class='form-control']"

# Priority 3: For attribute relationships
element_by_for = "//label[@for='ElementId']/..//input[@type='text']"

# Priority 4: Content-based (text, title, aria-label)
element_by_text = "//button[@type='button' and text()='Button Text']"
element_by_title = "//button[@title='Button Title']"
element_by_aria = "//button[@aria-label='Button Label']"

# Priority 5: Structural relationships
element_by_parent = "//div[@class='modal-content']//input[@name='ElementName']"
```

### 5. ELEMENT VARIANTS (MANDATORY)
```python
# Main element - Primary strategy
inp_element = "//input[@id='ElementId' and @name='ElementName']"

# Variants - Alternative strategies
inp_element_by_class = "//input[@name='ElementName' and @class='form-control']"
inp_element_by_for = "//label[@for='ElementId']/..//input[@type='text']"
inp_element_disabled = "//input[@name='ElementName' and @disabled]"
```

### 6. COMMENT STANDARDS (MANDATORY)
```python
# Element description - STABLE by [strategy/attribute]
element_name = "//xpath[@attribute='value']"
```

**Required Comment Format:**
- **Description** - What the element is
- **STABLE by** - What makes it stable (ID, name, class, for, content, etc.)
- **Additional context** if needed

### 7. DYNAMIC HELPER METHODS (MANDATORY)
```python
# ========== DYNAMIC HELPER METHODS ==========
@staticmethod
def get_element_by_value(value):
    """Get element by value - STABLE"""
    return f"//element[@value='{value}']"

@staticmethod
def get_element_by_text(text):
    """Get element by text content - STABLE"""
    return f"//element[text()='{text}']"

@staticmethod
def get_element_by_row_column(row, column):
    """Get element by row and column - STABLE"""
    return f"//table/tbody/tr[{row}]/td[{column}]"
```

### 8. MULTIPLE FALLBACK STRATEGIES (MANDATORY)
```python
# ========== MULTIPLE FALLBACK STRATEGIES ==========
@staticmethod
def get_element_all_strategies():
    """Multiple strategies for element - HIGHEST RELIABILITY"""
    return [
        "//element[@id='ElementId' and @name='ElementName']",
        "//element[@name='ElementName' and @class='form-control']",
        "//label[@for='ElementId']/..//element[@type='text']",
        "//div[@class='container']//element[@name='ElementName']"
    ]
```

### 9. VERIFICATION METHODS (MANDATORY)
```python
@staticmethod
def verify_page_loaded():
    """Verify page is properly loaded - STABLE CHECK"""
    return [
        "//element[contains(., 'Expected Text')]",
        "//button[@type='button' and @aria-label='Expected Label']",
        "//table//th[text()='Expected Header']",
        "//div[@class='expected-container']"
    ]

@staticmethod
def verify_page_closed():
    """Verify page is properly closed - STABLE CHECK"""
    return [
        "//element[@style='display: none;']",
        "//backdrop[@style='display: none;']"
    ]
```

